WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.310
You raised $360,000,

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:07.590
actually over $360,000

00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:09.640
for something that you came
up with all on your own

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:14.640
called COVID-19 Protest Relief Fund.

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:15.930
I wanna talk about this right away,

00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:17.950
'cause it's so important and inspiring.

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:19.403
Tell us what that fund does.

00:00:20.822 --> 00:00:23.740
It's basically a fund for protestors

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:27.040
who are out on the front
lines fighting in this,

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:30.840
what I call the uprising for
our justice and equality,

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:33.970
and in the midst of our pandemic

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:36.620
and putting their, risking
their bodies on the line,

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:39.270
some of them being in communities

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:41.410
that are already at high-risk.

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:43.897
And I was like, "Man, there
should be some kind of relief

00:00:43.897 --> 00:00:45.697
"for treatment, for some bills,

00:00:45.697 --> 00:00:47.540
"for some bill relief, for injuries,"

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:49.480
seeing all of the attacks
that were happening

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:53.010
on protestors just for
using their American right

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:54.390
to speak out.

00:00:54.390 --> 00:00:55.830
So, I just wanted to do something,

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:59.630
because I was having a bunch
of different conversations

00:00:59.630 --> 00:01:02.900
with folks and including
my family, who's high-risk,

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:05.730
so I couldn't be outside when
the protests were happening,

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:06.832
and I was like...

00:01:06.832 --> 00:01:07.665
And I usually am, so I'm like,

00:01:07.665 --> 00:01:10.177
"Damn, I kind of feel a little useless

00:01:10.177 --> 00:01:11.787
"in this whole movement.

00:01:11.787 --> 00:01:13.110
"I need to do something."

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:14.927
And I was like, "Man, there's
a lot of bodies out there.

00:01:14.927 --> 00:01:18.087
"Somebody should come up
with like a relief fund,

00:01:18.087 --> 00:01:19.400
"like somebody should do that."

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:21.890
And when I said somebody, I
meant like the government,

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:23.533
because it's like their jobs,

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:28.360
but I guess that was
like wishing too much.

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:30.100
So then I said that for like two weeks,

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:32.697
and then I was like, "Well,
why don't you do that?

00:01:32.697 --> 00:01:35.110
"Just start a GoFundMe,
people do it all the time."

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:36.720
I ain't never done a GoFundMe before,

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:40.301
so I just kind of googled how to GoFundMe,

00:01:40.301 --> 00:01:41.517
just went to the site, did it,

00:01:41.517 --> 00:01:44.380
and I was hoping that
it would maybe catch on,

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:46.352
some other people that were more prominent

00:01:46.352 --> 00:01:48.830
would do it and make...

00:01:48.830 --> 00:01:50.620
I didn't know we would
make that much money,

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:55.147
and by the fifth hour, we were
already like over $80,000,

00:01:56.150 --> 00:01:56.983
and I was like,

00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:59.697
"Oh man, I need to figure
out how to get this money

00:01:59.697 --> 00:02:00.790
"to the people,"

00:02:00.790 --> 00:02:02.300
'cause I don't play with
peoples' money, you know?

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:05.500
So, that became a three week crash course

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:08.250
getting to know organizers
across the country,

00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:10.015
getting to know activists,

00:02:10.015 --> 00:02:13.510
and learning what a non-profit
versus a mutual aid fund was,

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:15.480
which ours is a mutual aid fund,

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:17.880
and learning how it operates,

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:19.969
'cause my whole things was
getting the money to the people

00:02:19.969 --> 00:02:21.990
as quickly as we could.

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:23.570
But, I guess I had the best...

00:02:23.570 --> 00:02:24.730
I was in the best scenario

00:02:24.730 --> 00:02:28.010
where it's like usually you
start at a mutual aid fund

00:02:28.010 --> 00:02:30.460
or a not-for-profit and
then you try to raise money.

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:32.450
I had all the money and no knowledge,

00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:34.690
so between all the help and the organizers

00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:39.410
that really educated me on a
lot of things I needed to know,

00:02:39.410 --> 00:02:42.160
I was able to set it up and get it going,

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:45.500
and it's been really cool to
be on the other side of it now,

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:47.410
where the logistics are kind of worked out

00:02:47.410 --> 00:02:48.620
and now we're just trying

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:49.777
to get as much money out to the people

00:02:49.777 --> 00:02:52.580
and make as big a impact as possible.

00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:53.413
Good for you.

00:02:53.413 --> 00:02:54.246
I mean, God bless you.

00:02:54.246 --> 00:02:55.079
That's an amazing thing to do.

00:02:55.079 --> 00:02:56.559
I would think it would be kind of...

00:02:56.559 --> 00:03:01.559
I could see you being
panicked if $360,000 comes in

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:04.180
and you wanna get it to the people,

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:05.390
but there's this period of time

00:03:05.390 --> 00:03:06.800
where the money's just pouring in,

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:07.633
and you think like,

00:03:07.633 --> 00:03:09.360
"How do I get rid of this money?"

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:10.193
Yeah.

00:03:10.193 --> 00:03:11.220
Like being on Breaking Bad,

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:12.330
like there's money coming in,

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:14.341
I gotta get rid of this stuff.

00:03:14.341 --> 00:03:15.174
(laughs)

00:03:15.174 --> 00:03:16.683
Yeah, 'cause I was like...

00:03:16.683 --> 00:03:17.516
I was waking up like,

00:03:17.516 --> 00:03:20.637
"I gotta get rid of this,
'cause I'm just a comic, man.

00:03:20.637 --> 00:03:22.770
"I wanna make dick jokes, man."

00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:24.250
There were so many times, Conan,

00:03:24.250 --> 00:03:27.470
that I almost tweeted, I
bought a chain with it instead,

00:03:27.470 --> 00:03:28.642
just a joke.

00:03:28.642 --> 00:03:29.680
(laughs)

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:31.510
But, I was like I can't do this.

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:33.060
Until I figure out how to
do this, I can't make jokes

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:34.582
about it.
I know, I know.

00:03:34.582 --> 00:03:35.930
It's a funny joke,

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:37.744
but people would get
pissed off for a second.

00:03:37.744 --> 00:03:39.770
(laughs)

00:03:39.770 --> 00:03:43.750
Yeah man, but yeah it
was like a lot of stress,

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:46.880
'cause it was a world
I'm not familiar with.

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:48.660
But, I'm so glad I did it,

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:51.480
and on top of that, we've
worked with the Chicago Alliance

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:54.820
and the Black Lives Matter Chicago

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:56.390
and a bunch of other organizations,

00:03:56.390 --> 00:03:59.670
just getting masks to
people, taking care of tests.

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:01.240
We've been getting so many cool notes

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:02.820
about people like being
able to pay their rent,

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:03.653
because they're not behind,

00:04:03.653 --> 00:04:06.700
and just these medical bills
and there's a lot of people

00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:07.870
just getting beat up, man.

00:04:07.870 --> 00:04:09.860
A lot of people getting
beat up, a lot of phones,

00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:12.060
a lot of iPhones are
broken in the uprising.

00:04:12.910 --> 00:04:14.470
We've been able to take care of folks,

00:04:14.470 --> 00:04:16.460
and it's been the best...

00:04:16.460 --> 00:04:17.350
It's been a joy, man.

00:04:17.350 --> 00:04:18.850
It's been something that
brings a lot of light

00:04:18.850 --> 00:04:22.266
to what's been a stressful time
for me personally for sure,

00:04:22.266 --> 00:04:23.673
as everybody knows.

